  "question": "The main functions of the chain supermarket supply management system include:\n1. Supermarket Information Management: Each chain supermarket has a unique supermarket ID, also including supermarket name, supermarket address, and manager's phone number.\n2. Product Inventory Management: Each product has a unique product ID, recording product name, inventory quantity, and storage location.\n3. Distribution Department Information Management: Each distribution department has a unique department ID, including department name, department address, and manager's phone number.\n4. Purchase Order Management: Each purchase has a unique purchase ID, associated with a product ID, and records purchase date, supplier, purchase quantity, and other information.\n5. Payment Order Management: Each payment order has a unique order ID, linked to the purchase order ID, recording payment amount, payment date, and payment status.\n6. Supply Request Management: The system records the supply request information of each chain supermarket, using the supermarket ID, product ID, and request time as identifiers, linking supermarket and product information, recording the requested quantity.\n7. Distribution Management: The system generates a distribution notification, using the distribution notice number as the unique identifier, associated with the product ID and distribution department ID, recording distribution quantity, distribution time, and other information.\n\nThe specific business processes of the system are as follows:\nThe system records supply request information, including the product ID, quantity, request time, and supermarket information.\nWhen processing requests, the system queries the product inventory records. If the inventory satisfies the request, the system generates a distribution notification, including the distribution notice number, product ID, distribution quantity, distribution time, and distribution department information.\nIf the inventory is insufficient, the system records a stockout notification, and the purchasing department handles product procurement, the system records purchasing order information, including product ID, purchase quantity, supplier, purchase date, and payment information.\nOnce the purchase is completed, the qualified products are stored and the inventory is updated, the finance department records payment information based on the purchase order, including payment amount, payment date, and payment status. Through these records, the system can effectively manage supply requests, inventory status, distribution information, purchasing processes, and financial payments.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0456\nCREATE TABLE `supermarket` (\n  `supermarket_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `supermarket_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `supermarket_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `manager_phone` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supermarket_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `storage_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `distribution_department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `manager_phone` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `purchase_order` (\n  `purchase_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `supplier` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `other_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`purchase_id`),\n  KEY `purchase_order_ibfk_1` (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `payment_order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `purchase_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `payment_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  KEY `payment_order_ibfk_1` (`purchase_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `payment_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`purchase_id`) REFERENCES `purchase_order` (`purchase_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `supply_request` (\n  `supermarket_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `request_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `requested_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supermarket_id`, `product_id`, `request_time`),\n  KEY `supply_request_ibfk_2` (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `supply_request_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supermarket_id`) REFERENCES `supermarket` (`supermarket_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `supply_request_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `distribution_notice` (\n  `notice_no` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `distribution_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `distribution_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `other_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`notice_no`),\n  KEY `distribution_notice_ibfk_1` (`product_id`),\n  KEY `distribution_notice_ibfk_2` (`department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `distribution_notice_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `distribution_notice_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `distribution_department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
